namespace pdg { /**

\fn pdg::TileLayer::loadMapData(Uint8Array data, int mapWidth, int mapHeight, int dstX, int dstY)

\brief Load tile data from a Uint8Array into the specified region of the layer

This function loads tile data from a Uint8Array into a specific rectangular region of the TileLayer. The data is interpreted as a 2D array of tile indices.

\param data The Uint8Array containing the tile data to load
\param mapWidth The width of the tile map in the data (number of tiles horizontally)
\param mapHeight The height of the tile map in the data (number of tiles vertically)
\param dstX The X coordinate where to place the top-left corner of the loaded data in the layer
\param dstY The Y coordinate where to place the top-left corner of the loaded data in the layer

\details
The Uint8Array data should contain tile indices arranged in row-major order (left to right, top to bottom). Each tile index corresponds to a tile in the TileLayer's tile set.

The function will load the specified rectangular region from the data into the layer starting at the destination coordinates (dstX, dstY).

\warning The function will overwrite existing tile data in the destination region
\throws RangeError If the array contains fewer than mapWidth * mapHeight bytes.
\throws TypeError If data is not an attached, non-shared Uint8Array or MemBlock.
\note Tile indices in the data should be valid for the layer's tile set

\sa TileLayer::loadMapData(MemBlock, int, int, int, int)
\sa TileLayer::getMapData()
\sa MemBlock

**/ }